2acb23828f3117f290c41569eeb3bedc49d87fed8199106ea506","event_uuid":"280eb3ec-5839-4248-bcd8-a91793e2bdb1","position":{"commit_sha":"0a63b24cbe53cd03dd685d72c3ca01138d3a341a","position":"1787882672564020001-280eb3ec-5839-4248-bcd8-a91793e2bdb1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fee9a4b2645bc5c88378c7b23a20accd5cad2e43e8be3992ee5580106dd50359","event_uuid":"5917fe3d-6b1a-46f5-bd31-a3d03cf2b643","position":{"commit_sha":"e3b7308caa197874967b3ef6a4a0aa802f09dacf","position":"1787882678423457001-5917fe3d-6b1a-46f5-bd31-a3d03cf2b643"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7635fa0220fa3ea5f78ec136c77f0127dc8f30b93976f3eebdc2222fa61d7c21","event_uuid":"932e529d-be20-4ee7-9cc1-a1c07bd3477c","position":{"commit_sha":"ee0d96e519df47d32971cac045ce8f74dac9160e","position":"1787882682192044001-932e529d-be20-4ee7-9cc1-a1c07bd3477c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review BLOCK, correctly. AC1 offered three acceptable liveness forms and one of them — 'an asserted exit code' — cannot distinguish an executed-and-denied child from one that never launched, since a sandbox that fails to start also exits non-zero. That is precisely the ambiguity this ticket exists to remove, so offering it as sufficient would have let the fix reintroduce the bug.\n\nAC1 now requires liveness evidence produced BY THE CHILD after it started (a sentinel written to an allowed path, or a marker on stdout), asserted before the denial is read, and explicitly disqualifies the wrapper's exit status.","timestamp":1787879551651426001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed. Measured evidence for the false pass this ticket describes, using a wrapper mutated to launch nothing (`wrap()` returns /usr/bin/true):\n\n- OLD tests: 3 of the 4 enforcement tests PASSED, including test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied. Only test_write_inside_the_allow_list_succeeds failed, because it alone was inherently self-proving. So the denial tests reported success while the sandbox did nothing at all.\n- NEW tests, same broken wrapper: all 4 FAIL with 'the child never reached its write, so a denied/absent target proves nothing'.\n\nLiveness comes from an artifact the CHILD wrote after starting (a sentinel in the allow-list), asserted before the denial is read. Exit status is explicitly not used, since a sandbox that fails to launch also exits non-zero.\n\nBlast radius: denial is now proven with a create wherever possible. Only the incident-shape test removes anything, and it carries three independent bounds — Python asserts the target is strictly inside tmp_path; the path reaches the shell only as \"${TARGET:?}\" so an empty value aborts instead of globbing from the root; and the sandbox denies the unlink. The ${VAR:?} guard test contains NO destructive command: it asserts the shell never reaches a marker, because proving the guard by really running rm on an empty variable would perform the incident whenever the guard stopped working.\n\nRED proofs (all by real mutation): wrapper launching nothing -> 18 failed; unguarded $TARGET -> guard test failed; containment check disabled -> escape test failed. Gate classes: 1871 passed, 4 skipped.","timestamp":1787880805044998001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787855605495328001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eecc542d-5a50-4e47-9dff-f2e3e2285265","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"},{"link_uuid":"dfb5b709-e532-4023-956e-232948898301","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"485d-5973-c949-47fa"},{"link_uuid":"932e529d-be20-4ee7-9cc1-a1c07bd3477c","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe sandbox enforcement tests added by `e668-b496-e264-4283` in\n`tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py` assert only that a file is ABSENT after\nrunning a wrapped subprocess:\n\n```python\nassert not target.exists()          # denial \"proven\"\n```\n\nNothing asserts the sandboxed child actually launched and reached the write attempt.\nIf `sandbox-exec`/`bwrap` fails to start at all — bad profile, missing binary, a\nnamespace refusal, an argv regression — the write never happens, the file is absent,\nand the test PASSES. A total failure of the sandbox wrapper is indistinguishable from\ncorrect enforcement.\n\n`test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied` has the same shape in reverse: it asserts a\npre-existing `keep.txt` still exists. A sandbox launch failure trivially leaves the file\nin place, producing a false pass.\n\n## Why this matters more than a normal test gap\n\nThese are the ONLY tests that demonstrate the sandbox works. `e668`'s acceptance\ncriteria deliberately required observed enforcement rather than argv assertions,\nprecisely so the control could not be satisfied by construction alone. A test that\npasses when the mechanism is absent silently reintroduces the weakness those criteria\nwere written to exclude — the evidence for the whole feature rests on it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every enforcement test asserts positive LIVENESS of the sandboxed child through\n      an artifact the CHILD ITSELF produced after starting — a sentinel it wrote to an\n      ALLOWED path, or a marker it printed to stdout — asserted before the denial is\n      read. The wrapper's exit status does NOT qualify: a sandbox that fails to launch\n      also exits non-zero, so exit code cannot distinguish executed-and-denied from\n      never-ran, which is the exact ambiguity this ticket removes.\n- [x] The liveness assertion is proven load-bearing: with the sandbox mechanism forced\n      unavailable so the child never launches, the test goes RED rather than green.\n      Demonstrated by real substitution, not asserted.\n- [x] `test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied` gains the same liveness check, so a\n      launch failure cannot pass as \"the target survived\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria — blast radius\n\nAn enforcement test asserts that a control DENIES something. If the control silently\ndoes nothing, the denied action HAPPENS — which is the incident's own mechanism,\nre-created inside the test suite. These tests must therefore be fail-safe: a total\nsandbox failure must produce a red test, never damage.\n\n- [x] Write-denial is proven with a CREATE, not a DELETE, wherever the proof does not\n      require deletion. A leaked create is inert; a leaked delete destroys. Verified by\n      inspection: no enforcement test removes anything except the single incident-shape\n      test below.\n- [x] The incident-shape test is bounded so a TOTAL sandbox failure cannot escape the\n      pytest tmp dir. The target is passed via the environment and dereferenced as\n      `\"${VAR:?}\"`, so an empty or unset variable ABORTS the shell instead of expanding\n      to `rm -rf /*` — the exact guard whose absence caused the 2026-08-26 incident —\n      and the path is never interpolated into the shell string.\n- [x] Python refuses to launch the destructive child unless the target is non-empty,\n      absolute, and strictly inside `tmp_path`. Verified by a test asserting the\n      guard raises when handed a path outside `tmp_path`.\n- [x] The `${VAR:?}` guard is itself proven, not assumed: with the variable set empty\n      the shell aborts non-zero and the canary survives, asserted by a test that runs\n      that case WITHOUT a sandbox — so it demonstrates the guard alone is sufficient to\n      stop the incident's expansion.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- No enforcement test in the file can pass when the sandbox fails to launch.\n- Each liveness check is shown RED under a forced launch failure.\n- No enforcement test can damage anything outside the pytest tmp dir even if the\n  sandbox enforces NOTHING at all.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nFound by the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 2256 (patch sets 4 and 7; advisory, so\nit did not block the merge). Discovered from `e668-b496-e264-4283`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"add positive liveness assertions to every enforcement test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","485d-5973-c949-47fa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"280eb3ec-5839-4248-bcd8-a91793e2bdb1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c100-c4f1-2a2b-4905","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Sandbox enforcement tests pass when the sandbox fails to launch","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["40e48d66-7195-4f32-b6da-c888f629b835","81d510f4-4383-47f0-830c-a47fef53813e","169f9d03-9b96-47f8-b6d0-33ead832df33","5bb0f360-174c-4ec0-b2a8-7a8d009f9187","e09ea85a-874b-4d8f-8dea-776cdf439b77","557f6ac4-515b-4add-85ed-617a68c9fbb9","ece70bd2-18d6-43b1-aeb2-f824a8247e34","dfb5b709-e532-4023-956e-232948898301","6d5fc31e-4bfd-4634-b350-f245c8e401b2","280eb3ec-5839-4248-bcd8-a91793e2bdb1","5917fe3d-6b1a-46f5-bd31-a3d03cf2b643","932e529d-be20-4ee7-9cc1-a1c07bd3477c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787894820887836001,"uuid":"cfcbe783-19ee-4938-bb5f-3788eeec150e"}